%[text] %[text:anchor:T_ILPFC] # Design and Analyze an Interleaved Boost PFC Converter
%[text] An interleaved boost power factor correction (PFC) converter splits the single-phase line current between two legs switching 180 degrees apart, which cancels input ripple. This design solution shows how to size the power stage and select the semiconductors. The model uses the interleaved boost PFC plant and controller blocks from `ConverterLibrary`. You then simulate the closed loop, plot the AC, DC and per-leg waveforms, analyze the input-current harmonics, and estimate power loss and efficiency.
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_scope] ## Design Solution Scope
%[text] In this design solution, you:
%[text] - Size the power stage and review the estimated design parameters
%[text] - Select boost-leg and rectifier-bridge semiconductors that meet the required ratings
%[text] - Simulate the closed loop and inspect the AC input, DC output and per-leg waveforms
%[text] - Analyze the switching ripple and the line-frequency current harmonics (THD)
%[text] - Estimate power loss and efficiency \
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_sys] ## System Overview
%[text] The model comprises the Interleaved Boost PFC plant and controller. A diode bridge feeds two boost legs whose carriers are shifted by half a switching period. The legs share the line current and their ripple currents partly cancel at the input node.
%[text] The controller regulates the DC bus with an outer voltage loop that trims a power command. An inner current loop shapes the total inductor current into a rectified sine locked to the line. A differential balance loop equalizes the two leg currents without changing their sum.![](text:image:50f3)
modelName = "InterleavedBoostPFCConverter";
open_system(modelName);
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_design] ## Select Interleaved Boost PFC Converter Parameters
%[text] To design the power stage, use the `EstimateInterleavedBoostPFCParameters` live script. From your design requirements, it computes the per-leg boost inductance, the DC-bus capacitance, the ripple that survives interleaving and the required device rating, checked across the AC input range.
%[text] To open the parameter estimation workflow, enter this command in the MATLAB® Command Window:
%[text] ```matlabCodeExample
%[text] edit 'EstimateInterleavedBoostPFCParameters'
%[text] ```
%[text] Load the default parameters (AC input, DC bus reference, load power) and set the model name.
if ~exist('interleavedDesign','var')
    InterleavedBoostPFCDefaultInputParameters;
end
disp(table(designTable,'VariableNames',"Interleaved Boost PFC Estimated Design Parameters")); %[output:f636fae6]
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_selectcomp] ## Select Converter Components
%[text] This design solution rates the boost-leg and rectifier-bridge semiconductors and lists catalog parts that meet those ratings. The parts come from the Simscape™ parts feature.
%[text] To open the component selection workflow, run:
%[text] ```matlabCodeExample
%[text] edit 'SelectInterleavedBoostPFCComponents'
%[text] ```
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_op] ## Define the Operating Point
%[text] Set the DC bus voltage and the load power for the waveform, harmonic and loss analyses.
%[text] The waveform run covers 7.5 line cycles at a solver step that resolves the switching ripple, so the harmonic analysis reuses that run.
voltageReference = simscape.Value(interleavedDesign.outputVoltage.value, "V");  % DC bus setpoint (Vref)
outputLoadPower  = simscape.Value(interleavedDesign.ratedPower.value, "W");     % Output power (Pload)
rippleSpanMultiple = 5;                                                        % The ripple spectrum spans DC to this multiple of the switching frequency
maximumSolverStep  = 1/(2*rippleSpanMultiple*switchingFrequency.value);          % Solver step (s) that resolves that span
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_plot] ### Plot Simulation Result
%[text] To plot the converter waveforms, use `getConverterWaveforms`. It simulates the plant's `Simplified` variant.
%[text] The power factor and THD are measured from the input current. To set how many final line cycles are plotted, use `FocusCycles`.
simulationTime   = simscape.Value(150e-3, "s"); % Stop time of the waveform run, 7.5 line cycles at 50 Hz
[interleavedBoostPFCIVData, interleavedBoostPFCSimulationLog] = getConverterWaveforms(modelName, Converter="InterleavedBoostPFC", ... %[output:group:5a6b3593] %[output:18bd7020]
    Vref=voltageReference, Pload=outputLoadPower, ... %[output:18bd7020]
    SimTime=simulationTime, FrequencyHz=lineFrequency.value, FocusCycles=2, ... %[output:18bd7020]
    MaxStep=maximumSolverStep); %[output:group:5a6b3593] %[output:18bd7020]
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_harm] ### Harmonic Analysis and THD
%[text] To analyze the AC input current, use `estimateConverterHarmonics`. It reads the log of the waveform run above and plots:
%[text] - the broadband switching-ripple spectrum up to `RippleSpanMultiple` times the switching frequency
%[text] - the line-frequency harmonic stem through the 10th, THD in its title, then a THD-by-standard table (IEEE 519, IEC 61000). \
harmonicData = estimateConverterHarmonics(interleavedBoostPFCSimulationLog, Converter="InterleavedBoostPFC", ... %[output:group:7e94dfd0] %[output:8e7b3974] %[output:5a2f6ffc] %[output:0b592fa8]
    FundamentalHz=lineFrequency.value, SwitchingHz=switchingFrequency.value, ... %[output:8e7b3974] %[output:5a2f6ffc] %[output:0b592fa8]
    RippleSpanMultiple=rippleSpanMultiple, ... %[output:8e7b3974] %[output:5a2f6ffc] %[output:0b592fa8]
    ShowHarmonicTable=false); %[output:group:7e94dfd0] %[output:8e7b3974] %[output:5a2f6ffc] %[output:0b592fa8]
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_loss] ### Estimate Power Loss and Efficiency
%[text] To estimate the switching and conduction losses and the efficiency, use `getConverterPowerLoss`. It simulates the plant's `Detailed` variant.
%[text] A PFC's loss is averaged over whole line cycles. `MinCycles` sets how many line cycles at the end of the run are averaged; set `simulationTime` so the converter reaches steady state before them.
simulationTime   = simscape.Value(50e-3, "s");  % Stop time of the loss run, 2.5 line cycles at 50 Hz
lossData = getConverterPowerLoss(modelName, Converter="InterleavedBoostPFC", ... %[output:group:8082de21] %[output:050fcd69] %[output:600d265b]
    Vref=voltageReference, Pload=outputLoadPower, ... %[output:050fcd69] %[output:600d265b]
    SimTime=simulationTime, SwitchingLossDetail="lumped", ... %[output:050fcd69] %[output:600d265b]
    FrequencyHz=lineFrequency.value, MinCycles=1); %[output:group:8082de21] %[output:050fcd69] %[output:600d265b]
%[text] 
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_concl] ## Conclusion
%[text] This design solution sized an interleaved boost PFC power stage, selected its semiconductors, and reported its waveforms, harmonics and efficiency. The plant and controller are reusable `ConverterLibrary` blocks.
